  "limitations": "Decode is CPU measurement; LRU and sliding traces are memory simulations. Infeasible points have no generation timing or throughput. Pool budgets cover only owning K/V page arrays, excluding metadata, weights, gather and forward temporaries. Actual nbytes equals pages * block_size * bytes_per_token; unused budget is not fragmentation. Allocation microbenchmarks include Python management, not attention. Single-sequence lazy pages need not save memory versus T1 exact-size arrays. Tracemalloc peaks are auxiliary and miss some native allocations; RSS is a process lifetime peak. P0 tracing perturbs timing. Counterbalanced sequential orders share one process, without confidence intervals. This decode recipe stays within the window; fixture checks independently exercise full invalidation and rebuilding. Lookup hit rates include writes and per-layer block gathers; simulation hit rates refer to the synthetic trace and are not comparable generation hit rates."
}
